,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRepeat","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The repeat type represents repeat marks. The start of the repeat has a forward direction while the end of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"repeat has a backward direction. The times and after-jump attributes are only used with backward repeats that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are not part of an ending. The times attribute indicates the number of times the repeated section is played.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The after-jump attribute indicates if the repeats are played after a jump due to a da capo or dal segno.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/repeat":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/repeat","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"`repeat`"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLRepeat","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLRepeatV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"repeat","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/repeat","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The repeat mark associated with this barline."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"title":"MXLBarline","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}]}}}